Sval: remove Firefox chrome Sval never shows

The Firefox View and list-all-tabs buttons, the separator under the
bookmarks menu's toolbar item, the nav bar's private-browsing label and
pre-tabs spacer, the downloads panel's empty text, the urlbar search-mode
dropmarker, the bookmark star, the search one-offs, about:addons' Themes
category and about:support's Studies and Remote Experiments sections. Sval
replaces or drops each. Their readers outside tests take a missing element:
gTabsPanel.canOpen asks isElementVisible, which answers false for null;
FirefoxViewHandler reaches its button only from about:firefoxview, which
Sval does not build; CustomizableUI.buildArea skips a placed widget with no
node; BrowserPageActions.placeActionInUrlbar returns when an action's markup
node is missing; the categories box finds categories by name; the rest are
read by CSS alone. The star's other readers skip it where it is null.
UrlbarView builds no one-offs while scotchBonnet.disableOneOffs holds,
which is Firefox's default.

